[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Whether the runtime directory is reachable inside the agent sandbox is unmeasured

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SCRIBE-SOCKET-IN-SANDBOX
TITLE: Whether the runtime directory is reachable inside the agent sandbox is unmeasured
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Whether the user runtime directory is visible inside the agent sandbox jail is
unverified. If a jail does not carry /run/user, a client inside it cannot reach
a socket named there, and the escape hatch is a relative bind under the
worktree's own .devenv -- which is inside the bind-mounted tree by definition,
and whose path length stops mattering because a relative sun_path is a dozen
bytes.

Not designed around today: the harness owns daemon lifecycle in that world.
Measure it before the beads harness depends on either answer.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: MECH-BACKLOG-SCRIBE-DAEMON
  ROLE: Backlogged_In
